  "result": "I wrote the concept body and the three scenarios for `drv.motion.veering_right`, and the gate returned **OK** on the first run (1 of 6 used).\n\n**Body.** It requires three things at the observation, with `d` the lane's designated direction (`st_lane_direction c`) and `v` x's velocity (`kin_velocity x`):\n- **Moving:** x is moving, using `drv_motion_moving` with `speed_floor`.\n- **Forward:** the velocity's component along the lane is positive: `d.x·v.x + d.y·v.y > 0`.\n- **Right:** the cross product, with left positive, is below minus the tolerance times x's speed: `d.x·v.y − d.y·v.x < −(sine_tolerance · kin_speed x)`. Comparing with a product means nothing is divided by a measurement.\n\n**Witnesses.** Lane 100 points east; the instance sets `speed_floor` to 1 m/s and `sine_tolerance` to 1/10.\n- **holds:** x faces east but moves with velocity (8, −6) m/s at 10 m/s, so the cross product is −6, below −1.\n- **fails:** x moves with velocity (10, 0), parallel to the lane, so the cross product is 0.\n- **blind:** the same motion as `holds`, but the lane has no direction and `st.lane_direction` is masked.\n\n**Open choice.** I declared no narrowings. The contract says \"unknown where the carrier carries no designated direction\", and the body uses the ordinary three-valued \"and\". So when the direction is missing the result is unknown if x is moving, but false if x is not moving. The `blind` scenario has x moving, so it doesn't test the not-moving case. If the contract meant unknown in both cases, the body would need a `definedWhen` around it. I left that out because no atom says \"the direction is observed\".\n\n`task_result.md` is in the working directory and records the run, this choice and why I finished.",
